{% doc %}
  Renders the shared behavior for on-demand panels: drawers, popups and
  dropdowns built from a native `<dialog>` or `<details>` element.

  Wrap a single `<dialog id="...">` or `<details id="...">` inside a
  `<theme-panel>` element to make it openable/closable. Any element on the
  page can open or close a panel by id using data attributes:

    <button data-panel-open="cart-panel">Open cart</button>
    <button data-panel-close>Close</button>

  Put the `scroll-lock` attribute on the inner `<dialog>`/`<details>` when
  the panel should lock page scroll while open (drawers). Leave it off for
  lightweight, non-blocking panels (popups, dropdowns).

  This snippet renders no visible markup of its own, only the script tag
  for assets/theme-panel.js, so it's safe to render from multiple files:
  the component registers itself once however many times the script loads.

  @example
  {% render 'theme-panel' %}
{% enddoc %}

<script src="{{ 'theme-panel.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
